# Dependency Rules

Dependencies always flow downward.

Infrastructure

↓

Configuration

↓

Historical Data

↓

Storage

↓

Validation

↓

Dataset Builder

↓

Feature Engineering

↓

Target Generation

↓

Statistics

↓

Regime Detection

↓

Machine Learning

↓

Alpha

↓

Portfolio

↓

Execution

↓

Backtesting

↓

Monitoring

↓

Deployment

Reverse dependencies are forbidden.

Example

Portfolio may use Alpha.

Alpha may NOT use Portfolio.

Execution may use Portfolio.

Portfolio may NOT use Execution.

---

# Layer Responsibilities

Each package has exactly one responsibility.

Never mix responsibilities.

Example

exchange/

Only exchange connectivity.

Never feature engineering.

Never machine learning.

Never backtesting.

Example

features/

Only feature engineering.

Never execution.

Never order routing.

Never portfolio optimization.

---

# Package Isolation

Every package must be independently testable.

Every package exposes a public interface.

Internal implementation remains private.

Never import internal modules directly.

