# Architecture Constraints

Never create circular dependencies.

Never bypass architecture.

Never create shortcuts.

Never duplicate business logic.

Never hardcode configuration.

Never bypass validation.

Never bypass governance.

---

# Infrastructure Rules

Infrastructure knows nothing about

Market Data

Features

Models

Trading

Portfolio

Execution

Infrastructure provides

Logging

Configuration

Serialization

Hashing

Validation

Lifecycle

Metadata

Utilities

Nothing more.

---

# Data Layer Rules

Historical Data is immutable.

Raw data is append only.

Never modify raw datasets.

Derived datasets always create new versions.

Every dataset has

Metadata

Version

Schema

Hash

Lineage

Timestamp

---

# Research Rules

Research is reproducible.

Every experiment records

Dataset

Configuration

Parameters

Random seed

Code version

Commit hash

Results

Artifacts

No experiment is anonymous.

---

# Machine Learning Rules

Models never read exchange APIs directly.

Models consume research datasets only.

Every model has

Training metadata

Validation metadata

Version

Metrics

Artifacts

Promotion status

Rollback version

---

# Portfolio Rules

Portfolio construction never reads raw exchange data.

Portfolio consumes

Alpha

Risk

Capacity

Configuration

Nothing else.

---

# Execution Rules

Execution never predicts markets.

Execution consumes

Portfolio

Risk limits

Exchange connectivity

Cost models

Execution is deterministic.

---

# Testing Rules

Every module requires

Unit tests

Integration tests

Type checking

Documentation

Logging

Error handling

A module is incomplete without tests.

---

# Documentation Rules

Every public module explains

Purpose

Responsibilities

Inputs

Outputs

Dependencies

Exceptions

Configuration

Examples

---

# Configuration Rules

Never hardcode

Thresholds

Exchange URLs

API keys

Risk limits

Paths

Magic numbers

Everything belongs in configuration.

---

# Versioning Rules

Every artifact is versioned.

Datasets

Configurations

Policies

Models

Features

Reports

Strategies

Backtests

Everything is reproducible.

---

# Security Rules

Never expose secrets.

Never log API keys.

Never commit credentials.

Never store secrets in source code.

Always use environment variables or secret management.

---

# Performance Rules

Correctness before optimization.

Readability before cleverness.

Architecture before convenience.

Never optimize unverified code.

Benchmark before optimization.

---

# AI Development Rules

When implementing code

Never invent missing requirements.

If architecture is unclear

Stop.

Explain the ambiguity.

Ask for clarification.

Never guess architecture.

---

# Completion Rules

A task is complete only if

Architecture satisfied

Typing complete

Tests pass

Formatting passes

Linting passes

Documentation updated

Logging implemented

Error handling implemented

Configuration supported

Review completed

Only then is implementation complete.

---

# Non-Negotiable Principles

Architecture over convenience.

Evidence over assumptions.

Research before deployment.

Risk before capital.

Configuration over hardcoding.

Testing before merging.

Documentation before memory.

Institutional quality over rapid delivery.

These principles override all implementation decisions.